            v_{s+1}^* &= u_{s+1}^*-u_s^*
            =\underset{v\in\text{span}\Psi_{s+1}}{\arg\min} {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert u-v \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}-u_s^*\\
            &=\underset{v^\prime\in\text{span}\Psi_{s+1}}{\arg\min} {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert u-(u_s^*+v^\prime) \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}+u_s^*-u_s^*\\
            &=\underset{v^\prime\in\text{span}\Psi_{s+1}}{\arg\min} {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert e_s^*-v^\prime \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}.
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    Therefore, \eqref{equ:inequality} must hold.

For each stage \(s>0\), it is obvious that ${\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert u-u_{s}^* \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}\leq {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert u-u_{s-1}^* \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}$. In addition, we observe that \(u_{s-1}^*+{\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert u-u_{s-1}^* \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}/{\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert \psi_{s} \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}\cdot\psi_{s}\in\Psi_{s}\). According to the definition of \(u_{s}^*\), we have
    \[
